  "articleBody": "When a vehicle bumper, ladder, or water pipe damages your garage wall, deciding whether to patch a small section or replace full drywall panels depends on structural position and safety boundaries. Small punctures on an exterior-facing wall can often be patched neatly with a mesh backing and joint compound. However, if the impact punctures a fire-separation wall bordering your living room or bedroom, patching must preserve the integrity of the barrier.\n\nHow to Compare Your Options\nIf damage is confined to a localized area under twelve inches without structural moisture, a patch is economical and quick. But if the board is swollen from plumbing leaks, crumbles along the seams, or sits on a shared wall where panel integrity is compromised, replacing the full sheet is the right path. Never place a thin cosmetic patch over Type X drywall that protects the home from garage fumes or fire spread.\n\nWhen Professional Guidance Helps\nIf you see signs of damp insulation, hidden framing rot, or recurring water damage inside the wall cavity, professional evaluation keeps the problem from spreading. HH Remodeling LLC provides careful drywall repair, framing assessment, and surface finishing across Aurora and the Denver metro. Call 303-505-0866 or email Hhremodelingllc1986.ab@gmail.com to book an evaluation.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
